        {
            "language": "markdown",
            "source": [
                "##### Ejercicio Práctico 6: Renderizado Condicional y Listas \r\n\r\n**Objetivo** : Mostrar una lista de tareas y permitir agregar nuevas tareas.\r\n\r\n**Pasos** : \r\n1. **Crear el Componente `ListaTareas.js`** :"
            ],
            "outputs": []
        },
        {
            "language": "javascript",
            "source": [
                "import React, { useState } from 'react';\r\n\r\nfunction ListaTareas() {\r\n  const [tareas, setTareas] = useState(['Aprender React', 'Hacer la compra']);\r\n  const [nuevaTarea, setNuevaTarea] = useState('');\r\n\r\n  function agregarTarea() {\r\n    setTareas([...tareas, nuevaTarea]);\r\n    setNuevaTarea('');\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  return (\r\n    <div>\r\n      <h2>Lista de Tareas</h2>\r\n      <ul>\r\n        {tareas.map((tarea, index) => (\r\n          <li key={index}>{tarea}</li>\r\n        ))}\r\n      </ul>\r\n      <input\r\n        type=\"text\"\r\n        value={nuevaTarea}\r\n        onChange={(e) => setNuevaTarea(e.target.value)}\r\n      />\r\n      <button onClick={agregarTarea}>Agregar Tarea</button>\r\n    </div>\r\n  );\r\n}\r\n\r\nexport default ListaTareas;"
            ],
            "outputs": []
